From fb2398dd9bf8f95707979dc4587a6de930696cd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:43:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a park awaiting a card also re-probes when
 its status arrives by a replica rebuild or `kanban sync reconcile`

PR #2370 handed only the sync round's feed pull (`Pulled.status_changed`) to
kanban_awaited_card_wake.expedite (review 5894353204, t_01a1d5aec0e3a0c5). Two other replica
apply paths carried no status changes, so a park awaiting a card whose done status arrived on
them slept until its check_every (fail-safe, but up to 15 min), and the
awaited_card_done_park_lag warning was blind to it:

1. the snapshot rebuild on Resync (`Pulled(resync(...))` in `_pulled_replica`);
2. `kanban sync reconcile`: `backlog.replica_at_head -> _pull_replica` dropped
   `pulled.status_changed`.

Now:
- Rebuild: the old replica's card statuses are read before the file is dropped
  (`acw.statuses`) and diffed against the rebuilt replica (`acw.rebuilt`); the pages the failed
  pull applied before its Resync ride on the Resync (`acw.changes_page`) and count at their
  rebuilt status. The rebuilt Pulled carries the diff, so the round's existing expedite (and any
  standalone caller) sees it.
- Reconcile: `replica_at_head` forwards each chunk's `pulled.status_changed` to `expedite` on
  the live board.
- `report_lag` reads the awaited cards' status from the replica itself (throttled to once per
  60 s per board, nothing without a replica), so a status that arrived by any path is seen; a
  warned park is marked until it leaves scheduled, so it warns once, not once per scan.

No new probing: expedite still only moves an existing probe earlier on a status change, and the
30-minute quiet-window test still counts exactly the check_every probes.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_awaited_card_wake.py): a park awaiting X wakes within 60 s
when X->done arrives via a snapshot rebuild, and via `kanban sync reconcile` (plain and
compacted); the lag warning fires once for a status only the replica saw (`sync diff`'s
diagnostic pull); throttle, diff and Resync-carry units. RED on main: 7 failed (the 3 wake tests
fail on the wake assertion); GREEN: 21 passed.
